Date: Sun, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 6/17] bridge: mirror live PinMAME DMD into m_dmdFrame

VPM tables never push DMDPixels from script, so GetDmdFrame stayed empty
even with the script and PinMAME running. Pull the live dot-matrix frame
from the script's PinMAME controller (same 0..100 byte-per-dot scale the
script DMDPixels lane consumes) lazily on read, publishing only on change
so m_dmdFrameId stays a real change counter. Adds one narrow plugin
accessor; no new ABI surface, no script or table changes.

Target: vpinball/vpinball@64a480a96d1b972711fbb8eea014654c779b1e23

diff --git a/plugins/pinmame/PinMAMEPlugin.cpp b/plugins/pinmame/PinMAMEPlugin.cpp
index 55fbb86..8311f38 100644
--- a/plugins/pinmame/PinMAMEPlugin.cpp
+++ b/plugins/pinmame/PinMAMEPlugin.cpp
@@ -591,3 +591,26 @@ MSGPI_EXPORT void MSGPIAPI PinMAMEPluginUnload()
    PinmameSetMsgAPI(nullptr, 0);
    msgApi = nullptr;
 }
+
+// Headless WASM bridge: snapshot the live PinMAME dot-matrix display for
+// the WASM ABI. Pixels are bytes per dot in 0..100 (same scale the script
+// DMDPixels lane consumes). False when no VPM controller/DMD is active.
+bool PinMAME_GetDmdPixels(std::vector<uint8_t>& pixels, int& width, int& height)
+{
+   pixels.clear();
+   width = 0;
+   height = 0;
+   if (PinMAME::controller == nullptr)
+      return false;
+   width = PinMAME::controller->GetRawDmdWidth();
+   height = PinMAME::controller->GetRawDmdHeight();
+   if (width <= 0 || height <= 0)
+      return false;
+   pixels = PinMAME::controller->GetRawDmdPixels();
+   if ((int)pixels.size() < width * height)
+   {
+      pixels.clear();
+      return false;
+   }
+   return true;
+}
